45765	Q0	zis1	69	3.9824736	instruments_tools	The instrument covers individual aspects of working life and the general attitude to work. The 37 items represent four dimensions self realization resignation satisfaction with payment evaluation of the company.
45765	Q0	zis355	70	3.9196813	instruments_tools	The SECS GER is a German low threshold questionnaire for measuring political conservatism divided into the sub dimensions of economic and social conservatism. The scale comprises 12 items on political topics and is based on a cultural adaptation of the 12 Items of Social and Economic Conservatism Scale by Everett 2013 in order to provide a valid and reliable measuring instrument for the German context. The validation was carried out using two samples with comprehensive item analyses and tests of the psychometric properties. The tests for reliability of the total scale and the subscales showed acceptable to good results. Exploratory and confirmatory factor analyses supported the two factor structure and showed a model fit comparable to that of the American original whereby the cultural influence led to a different categorisation of two items. Construct and criterion validity are satisfactory.
45765	Q0	zis97	71	3.8615966	instruments_tools	The items documented here were used to measure the ALLBUS 96 theme Attitudes towards ethnic groups in Germany .
45765	Q0	zis263	72	3.8615775	instruments_tools	The article presents a measuring instrument for the multidimensional recording of the perception of study requirements. The instrument was developed on the basis of two qualitative preliminary studies that examine challenges in the initial study phase Bosse Trautwein 2014 Trautwein Bosse 2017 . The test analyses were carried out with a total sample of N 1907 students from various Bachelor s degree programmes at four universities. The final version of the measuring instrument comprises 21 items. The explorative factor analysis shows a six factor structure which was confirmed by a confirmatory factor analysis. Overall the subscales show a moderate to satisfactory measurement accuracy. Significant correlations with study success criteria provide indications of criterion validity of the developed measuring instrument.
45765	Q0	zis188	73	3.8047411	instruments_tools	With 15 short form or 20 long form items this scale measures consumers belief in the superiority of domestic over foreign products. This attitude is also called ethnocentrism of consumers and represents a further development of the concept of ethnocentrism against the background of consumer research. According to Jacobys 1978 it is assumed that the superiority of domestic products goes beyond purely functional aspects and includes economic social and moral considerations. In concrete terms this means that ethnocentric consumers are convinced that it is not right to buy foreign products because this attitude damages the domestic economy and causes unemployment.
45765	Q0	zis273	74	3.7957041	instruments_tools	This paper presents the validated German language version of the team processes survey measure. The team processes framework introduced by Marks et al. 2001 serves as the theoretical basis. Analogous to the English scale Mathieu et al. 2019 the German language version of the team processes survey measure is available in a long version 30 items and a short version 10 items . The factor structure derived from the team processes framework can be confirmed for both versions. Furthermore substantial relationships between the different team processes and common team level constructs e.g. cohesion group potency and multiple indicators for team effectiveness are indicators for both convergent construct validity and criterion validity of the instrument. Both the long and the short versions of the team processes survey measure have a high psychometric quality.
45765	Q0	zis6	75	3.7864826	instruments_tools	The seven instruments for recording socio political activities and attitudes developed by scientists from the Social Science Institute of the Federal Armed Forces SOWI relate to these areas Political Alienation Social Isolation Politics as a Disruptive Factor Apolitical Attitudes Power of Disposal Political Commitment and Anomie.
45765	Q0	zis190	76	3.758027	instruments_tools	This scale measures the subjective perception of conflict groups with 15 items. According to Anthony Giddens model class conflicts are classified on the second level of class consciousness. The scale is intended to record how conflicts of interest between different groups are perceived.
