2741	Q0	zis141	95	2.8490694	instruments_tools	The present scale records reasons for postponing learning. The scale covers the areas mental distraction and alternative activities and was developed as part of a research project on procrastination at the University of Münster.
2741	Q0	dbd-13	96	2.847724	instruments_tools	This guide outlines the steps for accessing the YouTube Data API v3 and using it as a tool for research. We explain how to create a dedicated Google account a project on the Google Cloud Console and access credentials for authentication. We also give examples for basic functionalities like sending GET POST requests with specific parameters to retrieve data and discuss the limitations of working with YouTube APIs. The guide is written for social science researchers who are interested in using the YouTube Data API v3 for data collection and do not yet have extensive experience in programming or working with APIs. Note For an overview of more approaches and tools that can be used for collecting YouTube data please also consider this overview guide on working with YouTube data.
